510338 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c4202d35-11cb-528d-8f7b-8baa57144892" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510447 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186510316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510447 #edb/ref 1069 "q-157078" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510447 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510447 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the QR decomposition $A=QR,$ find the least-squares solution to $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nQ=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{70}}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5} & 3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{5} & -5\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,R=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{70}}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510447 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c07b8d08-df25-5edc-8755-7d7271698aeb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510447 #edb/ref 1074 "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting our matrices, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{70}}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]}}x & =\\overset{{Q}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{70}}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 3\\sqrt{5} & 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 3\\sqrt{2} & -5\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]x & =[\\begin{aligned}-10\\sqrt{5} \\\\ -10\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5}{x}_{1}+2\\sqrt{5}{x}_{2} &=-10\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{2}{x}_{2} &=-10\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-10.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5}{x}_{1}+2\\sqrt{5}(-10) & =-10\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5}{x}_{1} & =10\\sqrt{5} \\\\ {x}_{1} & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the least-squares solution to $Ax=b$ is $[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186510486 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186510507 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510486 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1c7fbdd9-d70e-53c6-9583-045def1fb610" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510486 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186410811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510507 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "58faa96e-dfec-57d8-91b9-fd2fd0bd774a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510507 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186510447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510555 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186510559 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510555 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e98b958c-ff8a-5dac-9009-16dbadd67c04" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510555 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186510449 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510559 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186510562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510559 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "eeaed52a-85d1-5761-bbe1-bcc1658b24ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510559 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186510454 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510562 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186510486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510562 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f8407afd-1563-5fa7-a7c0-218f08f7c276" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510562 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186510364 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559046 #edb/ref 1080 "$x$ and $\\frac{1}{‖b‖}\\cdot b$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559046 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 